{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D547|D397|D436|D411|ladder|reference' /Users/lchingen/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"16:## User preferences\n79:## User preferences\n136:## User preferences\n169:## User preferences\n176:- Step 2 exploratory retrieval on 282 items found about 90% of reference targets at top-10 using thesis+evidence embeddings, 95.9% evidence-only, versus 82.1% production lexical retrieval. Only three cross-thesis positives were available. Forward simulation yielded 180 records, 102 merges, roughly two clear wrong merges plus six arguable and 14 missed repeats. [Task 1]\n183:- Exploratory retrieval percentages are not production accuracy: references were exploratory and cross-thesis positives sparse. The reader test used fixed simulated decisions, with no live writer/database or Step 4; do not call it end-to-end or infer wrong-group safety. [Task 1]\n200:## User preferences\n234:## User preferences\n243:- Handoff begins at `/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/claude-handoff-2026-11-05/README.md`; the ~95 MB archive has stopped-run state, source items, databases, raw requests/answers, frozen-ruler references, worktree diffs and checksums. All 2,236 manifest files verified. It is a local-path-dependent snapshot, not a portable runnable checkout; review paid-call scripts before running. [Task 2]\n268:## User preferences\n308:## User preferences\n343:## User preferences\n383:## User preferences\n426:## User preferences\n469:## User preferences\n477:- In D254, three of 582 reference fields were lexically invalid, but whole-answer writer rejection blocked 63 records. Treat this as writer-contract failure amplification, not proof that 63 records were semantically wrong. [Task 1]\n478:- Before another comparison, use an unseen full article, prewrite the reference before seeing output, blind the evaluator to arm identity, and exercise the actual downstream reader/selector. [Task 1]\n501:## User preferences\n544:## User preferences\n574:## User preferences\n626:## User preferences\n669:## User preferences\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '## D397|## D436|## D411|## D547' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"4326:## D397 · 2026-11-10 · A topic that asks more than one thing gets one judged question; the other parts are shown as not judged\n4530:## D411 · 2026-11-10 · An amount already reported may be the baseline of a ladder, labelled as that and never as the market's expectation\n4847:## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it\n6698:## D547 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the audit of line 2 finds an undefined term; the description-only reading is refused; the recount against D397, D436 and the July rulings opens no prompt change (council consensus)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '315,390p' clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py\"","aggregated_output":"            {'label': 'Ruled out',\n             'condition': f\"{ruled_out}{'' if ruled_out.endswith('.') else '.'} This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of \"\n                          f'rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after {article_day} and '\n                          f'stands on {due_day}, and only when rung 1 does not.'},\n            {'label': 'Still open', 'condition': f'Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on {due_day}.'}]\n\n\ndef write_view(ladder, passage, *, thesis, article_day, company, research_list):\n    \"\"\"The view an accepted ladder is written as: its object, kind, focus, question, year, due day and its rungs in position\n    order, each with the label and condition the judge is shown and, for a figure, its bounds as floats.\"\"\"\n    object_id = research_list.resolve(ladder['object'])\n    object_kind = research_list.kind(object_id)\n    reference = ladder.get('reference')\n    reference_status = None\n    if ladder.get('event') is not None:\n        rungs = event_rungs(ladder['event'], ladder['due_day'], article_day)\n        year = ladder['due_day'][:4]\n    else:\n        figure = ladder['figure']\n        ascending = sorted_ranges(figure['ranges'])\n        middle_text_suffix = ' (no reference figure when the question opened)'\n        reference_status = 'no reference figure'\n        if reference is not None and reference['value'] is not None:\n            if reference['kind'] == 'last_reported':             # D411: named as that, never as what the market expects\n                middle_text_suffix = f' (the amount last reported when the question opened: \"{passage}\")'\n                reference_status = 'last reported figure'\n            else:\n                middle_text_suffix = f' (the reference when the question opened: \"{passage}\")'\n                reference_status = 'reference figure'\n        in_position_order = list(reversed(ascending)) if (object_kind == 'company' and figure['favourable_end'] == 'higher') else ascending\n        rungs = []\n        for position, bounds in enumerate(in_position_order, start=1):\n            condition = interval_text(bounds['lo'], bounds['hi'], figure['unit'])\n            label = COMPANY_LABELS[position - 1] if object_kind == 'company' else condition\n            if bounds is ascending[2]:\n                condition += middle_text_suffix\n            rungs.append({'label': label, 'condition': condition,\n                          'lo': None if bounds['lo'] is None else float(bounds['lo']), 'hi': None if bounds['hi'] is None else float(bounds['hi'])})\n        year = figure['year']\n    return {'object_id': object_id, 'object_kind': object_kind, 'kind': 'asset' if object_kind == 'company' else 'theme',\n            'looks_at': thesis['outcome'], 'question': ladder['question'], 'due_day': due_day_of(ladder, object_kind, object_id, research_list),\n            'year': year, 'rungs': rungs,\n            'reference_status': reference_status}\n\n\n# ---- check 8: one thesis, one or two requests -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef user_text(payload, closing_text):\n    \"\"\"The user text of the request: the payload as one JSON object, a blank line, the closing check.\"\"\"\n    return json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n\\n' + closing_text\n\n\ndef ladder_for_thesis(payload, *, system_text, closing_text, schema, call_model, check):\n    \"\"\"Ask for one thesis's ladder; send a refused answer back once, with the answer itself and the reasons, so that the model\n    corrects what it wrote and does not start again. Returns the outcome record.\n\n    `call_model(system_text, user_text, schema)` sends one request and returns a dict with `answer_text` (the model's own text, or\n    None when the response carried none), `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `request_sha256`, `cached` and `error` (None, or the\n    reason the answer could not be read or did not fit the schema). `check(answer)` returns (reasons, passage) as `check_answer`\n    does, with the thesis and its article bound in. A cached answer raises CachedAnswer.\n    \"\"\"\n    requests = []\n    note = ''\n    for _ in range(2):\n        sent = call_model(system_text, user_text(payload, closing_text) + note, schema)\n        if sent.get('cached'):\n            raise CachedAnswer(f\"thesis {payload['thesis']['id']}: the model archive answered from its cache\")\n        record = {'request_sha256': sent['request_sha256'], 'answer_text': sent['answer_text'], 'input_tokens': sent['input_tokens'],\n                  'output_tokens': sent['output_tokens']}\n        reasons, answer, passage = [], None, None\n        if sent['error']:\n            reasons = [sent['error']]\n        else:\n            try:\n                answer = parse_exactly(sent['answer_text'])\n            except (ValueError, RecursionError) as error:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/proofs/audit-cases.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"event_reference_cases_failed_or_open\": [\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n   \"case\": \"u1/clean-11\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will China's government approve imports of Nvidia's H200 AI chips into China — and roughly how many — enabling Nvidia to begin generating H200 revenue in the country?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Whether Chinese authorities grant approval for Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek and other firms to import Nvidia H200 chips (potentially a total below 200,000), as reflected in official Chinese government decisions and in Nvidia's disclosed China H200 revenue.\",\n    \"period\": \"Nvidia's current fiscal year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027), checked at its next annual report/10-K; set by the rule that a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n    \"sentence\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site.\\nChinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\\nThe companies need to say how many chips they need – and why – to get approval, according to the Information.\\nThe chips have emerged as a geopolitical flas\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities officially approve at least one application by Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek, or another Chinese firm to import Nvidia H200 chips into China by January 31, 2027?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 2,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The reference is null even though the article reports that China plans to allow limited H200 purchases.\",\n      \"XR: the reference is null although the article states 'China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips', a stated plan.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 3,\n     \"reference_words\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n   \"case\": \"u1/clean-6\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Rubin Ultra rack-scale platform — the Kyber NVL144 architecture that houses 144 Rubin Ultra GPUs — reach first shipments in 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform reaches first shipments (the step that brings revenue) in 2027 or is delayed to 2028.\",\n    \"period\": \"2028 — the release date SemiAnalysis reports Kyber has been pushed to from an original 2027; the question is settled when Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra first ships (the item supports the original-2027-vs-2028 timing).\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia pushes Kyber release to 2028 following manufacturing concerns – report\",\n    \"sentence\": \"The Kyber server cabinets, which have been designed to house 144 Rubin Ultra GPUs connected via the company’s NVLink 7 Switch, had originally been slated for release in 2027.\\nKyber allows GPUs to be mounted in compute trays that sit vertically rather than horizontally, a design that Nvidia has described as being “like books on a shelf,” and which reportedly boosts density and reduces latency.\\nHowever, the research firm claimed that issues in manufacturing the printed circuit board (PCB) midplane that connects the modules together have caused the setback.\\n“Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has bee\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform make its first shipments during calendar 2027, as established by an NVIDIA shipment confirmation or a SemiAnalysis follow-up report?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": \"had originally been slated for release in 2027\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 2,\n     \"reference_words\": \"had originally been slated for release in 2027\",\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"holds\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n      \"holds\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"mark\": \"open\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The reference quotes a 2027 release plan but omits its stated year, and the 2028 due date leaves a 2027 shipment question open for an extra year.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 3,\n     \"reference_words\": \"pushing its release date to 2028\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n   \"case\": \"u3/clean-3\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform, the product line that carries its data center value, begin shipping by a check date (end of calendar 2026)?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Confirmation that first Vera Rubin shipments have begun, versus slipping into 2027 or later.\",\n    \"period\": \"First shipments by end of calendar 2026 — set by the item: the platform 'could begin shipping later this year' in an article dated 2 July 2026.\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"sentence\": \"Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform by December 31, 2026, as determined from NVIDIA earnings releases and Form 10-Q disclosures and first-shipment confirmations from NVIDIA or its server and system partners?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 2,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The article says Vera Rubin could begin shipping later this year, but the reference is null.\",\n      \"XR: the reference is null although the article states the expected timing in words (Vera Rubin 'is in full production and could begin shipping later this year'), which the field should quote with kind expected and no number.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 3,\n     \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n   \"case\": \"u3/clean-9\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices with an adverse decision, fine or remedy, and by when?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"The French competition authority's conclusion of its antitrust probe into Nvidia's alleged anti-competitive conduct in cloud-AI and GPU markets, including the decision date, finding and any fine or remedy imposed.\",\n    \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027) — set because a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end; the item reports the probe is 'nearing a conclusion.'\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n    \"sentence\": \"Regulators are simultaneously intensifying their oversight, with the French competition authority announcing Thursday that its antitrust investigation into the company is nearing a conclusion.\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 2,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"holds\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"holds\"\n     ],\n     \"mark\": \"open\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"XR: the reference is null although the article states the authority announced its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', an expectation stated in words.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 3,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"mark\": \"holds\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"July\",\n   \"case\": \"c1/clean-14\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will France's competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets and issue a decision (fines or remedies) by Nvidia's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"A final decision by the French competition authority on its antitrust probe into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices.\",\n    \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (Nvidia's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory decision 'nearing a conclusion' with no date of its own)\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n    \"sentence\": \"Regulators are simultaneously intensifying their oversight, with the French competition authority announcing Thursday that its antitrust investigation into the company is nearing a conclusion.\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets by 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"holds\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The article reports the authority's own announcement that its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', an expectation for this event that the reference should quote, yet the reference is null.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 2,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"holds\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"XR: the article reports the French competition authority announcing that its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', which is the authority's own stated expectation in words, yet the reference is null.\"\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 3,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"holds\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The article says the authority announced its investigation is 'nearing a conclusion', which states an expectation in words, yet the reference is null.\"\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"reading\": \"July\",\n   \"case\": \"c1/clean-3\",\n   \"thesis\": {\n    \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin shipping by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n    \"outcome\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin to customers, confirmed by NVIDIA.\",\n    \"period\": \"2026-12-31 (the item says shipping could begin later in 2026, from a 2026-07-02 article)\",\n    \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n   },\n   \"article\": {\n    \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"sentence\": \"Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\"\n   },\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that first shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform to customers have begun by December 31, 2026, through a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing?\",\n   \"attempts\": [\n    {\n     \"attempt\": 1,\n     \"reference_words\": null,\n     \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n      \"fails\",\n      \"fails\"\n     ],\n     \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n     \"mark\": \"fails\",\n     \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n      \"The article says Vera Rubin could begin shipping later this year, but the expected reference is null.\",\n      \"The article says Vera Rubin 'could begin ship