ned by the due day; it is ruled out by the due day though it has not happened\n43-  (decided against, or formally abandoned or withdrawn); neither. The step writes the first condition and, when something can\n44-  rule the event out, the way it names for that; the rest is code's, so every outcome has exactly one rung. An event that has\n--\n49-  closing decision, with or without a penalty, is `Yes`; the authority formally abandoning or withdrawing the proceeding without\n50-  that decision or conclusion is `Ruled out`; the proceeding still going on the due day is the last rung (D420). A\n51-  difference inside an outcome (an approval with conditions against one without) is not a rung; when the thesis's wording names\n52:  it, it belongs in `not_judged`. A figure has five ranges,\n53-  and exactly one holds for every value: no overlap, no gap.\n54-- A question about the company's revenue, profit, share, product progress or its own obligations is the company's (object NVDA,\n55-  kind asset). A question about what happens in the world (licensing, aggregate spending, a policy) is a theme's. A question\n--\n59-  fine), the question is the company's (D418).\n60-- A company's figure runs from Strongly bullish to Strongly bearish, meaning good or bad for the company's business. An event's\n61-  rungs carry no such labels.\n62:- The reference is what the question is measured against when it opens. Its kind is `expected` for what the market expects: a\n63-  consensus, the company's guidance, a stated plan or deadline. For a figure, where the article states no expectation and gives\n64:  the amount most recently reported for the same quantity, that amount is the reference and its kind is `last_reported`; a\n65-  reported amount is never called an expectation (D411). When the article states a number, the field carries it and a\n66-  figure's middle rung holds it; a stated range is carried by its two ends, and the middle rung runs from at or below its lower end to at or above its upper end. When the\n67-  article states it in words alone, the field carries the words and no number, and the ranges are the step's own estimate.\n--\n92-| field | values | the mark |\n93-|---|---|---|\n94-| `item` | the item number | |\n95:| `Q` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the judged question is worded as a question, not as an assertion, and asks the thing the thesis's `outcome` names. For a figure it also names the period the figure covers, or the day it is measured at, and the material that settles it. And it does not ask something other than its `focus` line (a focus that also names parts listed in `not_judged` is expected and is not a conflict). It can be understood by a reader who never sees the article: it never says \"this item\" or leans on a figure or a name it does not give. A group named as the trade names it (\"the big four AI hyperscalers\", \"the top five hyperscalers\") is a name the question gives: a question is not failed for not listing the group's members. `n/a` for a `no_ladder` |\n96-| `O` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the object is the question's own company or the right theme, by the rule above: a tracked government decision on a class of products is the theme's; the company's own sales under it, and a proceeding against the company, are the company's |\n97-| `R` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | exactly one rung holds for every outcome. For a figure: the ranges meet end to end. For an event, where code writes the last rung: the `Yes` condition is the event the question asks about; the first sentence of the `Ruled out` condition, when there is one, is a decision against that event as a whole, or its abandonment or withdrawal as a whole, taken after the article's day and standing on the due day, and not the event's merely being still awaited, the refusal of one part of it, or a bar already in place when the article appeared (it need not list every way: code's sentence takes the others); and where the event can plainly be ruled out before the due day (a formal refusal, a block, an announced abandonment; for an authority's proceeding, its formal abandonment or withdrawal without the asked-for decision or conclusion) and the answer has no `Ruled out` rung, the mark fails; it fails too when `ruled_out_by` names no one who decides, or when the decision named is the day arriving, the event not having happened, or a decision to go on with a proceeding. Every condition is concrete and can be checked on the due day: none rests on a target or a threshold that is not yet set |\n98-| `D` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the due day follows the rule for its kind. A figure: the day the thesis or the article states, or, where neither states one, the day code sets from the year the figure covers (60 days after the company's fiscal year-end; 90 days after the calendar year-end for a theme's figure), which holds when the figure asked for is that year's figure. An event: the date the thesis or the article gives for assessing it, or the last day of the period it names, or the company's fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision with no date. It fails when the day contradicts a date the thesis or the article gives, falls before the figure's period ends, or, for an event, is a date none of these gives And `due_day_basis` says truly where the day comes from: `stated` only when the thesis or the article gives that day; `period_end` only when it is the last day of the period the thesis names, or the fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision; `expected_publication` when the step set the day it expects the figure to be published. For a thesis whose `opens_as` is binding_obligation: an obligation already taken on is due at its next annual filing, and one not yet signed on the day by which the signing can be checked; another day fails |\n99:| `X` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | a figure: a number the `reference` carries lies in the middle rung, as the judge will read it (for a stated range: the middle rung runs from at or below its lower end to at or above its upper end); a reference with no number, or none, has nothing to place and holds, unless the ladder presents as expected something the article does not state. An event: the ladder presents as expected only what the article states |\n100-| `F` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a company's figure only: the direction is defensible (which end is bullish), and the reason given in `favourable_why` supports the favourable end. For an amount the company owes, guarantees or has committed to pay, where neither the thesis nor the article settles which end is good for the business (they argue both ends or say nothing on it), the lower end is the favourable one (D413), and \"higher\" fails unless the thesis's own words say that more of it is good. `n/a` for an event and for a theme |\n101-| `Y` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a figure only: the year, the unit and the scale of the numbers are the question's (an amount in full; a percentage as 31, not 0.31), and the figure is a whole year's. A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year fails, whatever the thesis asks |\n102-| `G` | `holds`, `fails`, `not_assessable`, `n/a` | for a figure, always one of the first three: where the article gives any figure for this quantity, `holds` when an analyst would accept the ranges as a fair division of the outcomes around it and `fails` when not; `not_assessable` when the article gives none. `n/a` only for an event's ladder and for a `no_ladder` |\n103:| `L` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | every other part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) is listed in `not_judged`, each with a reason that says why it is left out; a wording that asks nothing else holds with an empty list |\n104:| `B` | a list | exactly one entry for each part listed in `not_judged`, in its order: `\"bet\"` when an analyst would hold a separate view on it, `\"not_a_bet\"` when it is a detail of the judged question; `[]` when nothing is listed and for a `no_ladder` |\n105:| `XR` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the `reference` field quotes what the article states the market expects, with `kind` `expected`, or, for a figure where the article states no expectation, the amount most recently reported for the same quantity (the same thing measured the same way: not a part of it, a ceiling on it or another quantity), with `kind` `last_reported`; the kind says truly which. It carries the number when the article states one (a range by its two ends), and no number the article does not state. It is null only when the article states no expectation and, for a figure, no amount last reported for the same quantity either; an event's is null whenever the article states no expectation |\n106-| `N` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a `no_ladder` only: the refusal is justified by one of the allowed cases, and that case truly applies. A refusal because the question belongs to another company or to a matter no listed theme covers names that company or matter. Which year is this year and which next year is read from the `fiscal_year_note` |\n107-| `W` | a string | any other fault that would mislead a reader of this judged question, in a short sentence; the empty string `\"\"` when there is none. The field is always present |\n108-| `why` | a string | one sentence giving the reason for every `fails` and for a non-empty `W`, naming the words or the figure; it may be empty only when no mark fails and `W` is empty |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '4326,4352p;4530,4555p;4847,4875p;6698,6745p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D397 · 2026-11-10 · A topic that asks more than one thing gets one judged question; the other parts are shown as not judged\n\n- **Asked**, after the review council on the Step 4 design (round log §69; two blind readers found 12 to 16 of the 34 opened theses\n  asking more than one thing): \"新系统自己开的 34 道题里，有 12–16 道一题问了两件事（例如：英伟达会不会给 OpenAI 的俄亥俄数据中心签担保——金额多少？）。给这种题写答案分段时，怎么处理？\"\n  - Options:\n    - judge only the main thing and show the rest as not judged (recommended). The option stated its costs: those parts have no\n      answer for now; three memory topics with no main part get no answer; and it departs from his 2026-10-20 rule that a question\n      looks at one thing and two things are two questions (D38), recorded as a gap to fill;\n    - split into two questions, each judged, as D38 says;\n    - do not judge such a topic until Step 1 opens it as one thing.\n  - Alex: \"只判主要那件 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided:**\n  - In the clean Step 4's ladder step, a thesis gets at most one judged question: the part its `outcome` names. Every other part of\n    its wording is listed and shown beside the answer as not judged.\n  - A thesis with no main part gets no judged question, with the reason recorded.\n  - For a topic that holds two real bets this departs from D38 until splitting is built. It is an open defect, sized by the first\n    test: readers mark each part left out as a bet an analyst would hold or not.\n- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step only. D38 stands for production.\n\n## D398 · 2026-11-10 · The clean ladder step carries D186: ranges against the reference, the favourable end registered, labels by code\n\n- **Asked**, with the census of production's own ladders (one request, the same in three draws, gave three different ladders, one\n  with its direction reversed): \"你 10 月 26 日定过、11 月 5 日说“我们要做”的那条规矩还没实现：答案分段要对着市场预期或公司指引写成“高于／接近／低于”，并且每道题登记“数字越高对公司是好还是坏”。新做的“定档”这一步要不要直接带上它？\"\n  - Options:\n    - both halves here (recommended). The option stated its costs: 7 to 9 of 18 number questions have no reference figure in their\n      opening article, so their ranges are the model's estimate and are marked \"no reference\"; a direction can still be registered\n      wrong, which the first test measures;\n## D411 · 2026-11-10 · An amount already reported may be the baseline of a ladder, labelled as that and never as the market's expectation\n\n- **Asked:** \"文章只给了“已经公布的数字”（例如英伟达现有采购承诺 1190 亿美元），没有说市场预期明年是多少。这个已公布的数字能不能用来当分档的比较基准？现在模型把它填进了“市场预期”一栏，两家读者都判这是错的。\"\n  - Options: usable when labelled (recommended): \"可以拿来当基准，但明确标成“最近一次已公布的数字”，不再叫“市场预期”；文章给的是区间（如 50%–60%）时也允许填区间。这需要改答案格式，我会放在事件题之后单独做、单独验证。\"; not usable (a reference only when the article states an expectation).\n  - Alex: \"能用，但要标明 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided:** the reference of a figure may be the amount last reported, when the article states no expectation; it is then\n  named as the last reported amount, to the judge and to readers, and never as what the market expects. A reference the\n  article states as a range is carried as a range. This changes the answer's shape; it is built and measured after the event\n  answers (D408), on its own.\n- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n\n## D412 · 2026-11-10 · Every round is reflected on in the council to a recorded consensus, then the next test goes straight ahead; every trace is read by Claude itself\n\n- **Alex's words** (set as the session's goal while the second Stage A of the clean ladder step was being sent): \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace。现在重新的总结我们的目标，做到哪里了，我们再改么，离生产还有多远\".\n- **Decided:** after each round of work (a probe, a measurement, a change of design), Claude writes its own reflection, has the\n  council read the record cold and challenge it, and reaches a consensus or writes down what remains disputed; the consensus is\n  recorded; the next test then goes ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with no further rounds of review for their\n  own sake. Claude reads every trace itself and does not rest on readers' marks alone. When asked where the work stands, the\n  answer gives the goal, what is done, whether things are still being changed, and the distance to production.\n- **Done on the day:** written into AGENTS §7.3 at the council rule, in his words; a reflection council on the whole Step 4\n  record (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ja-*`, `jb-*`) reached a consensus recorded in the round log §69; all\n  132 answers of the second Stage A read by Claude before any reader's row.\n- **Scope:** how the work is run, every module.\n\n## D413 · 2026-11-10 · Where the texts do not settle it, an amount the company owes or guarantees is registered with the lower end favourable\n\n## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it\n\n- **Asked**, after two blind source readers agreed on none of six cases (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/PREREAD-RESULT.md`):\n  \"例子：同一篇文章里有'2027 年 HBM 出货增长多少'和'2027 年 HBM 是否仍然供不应求'。两位读者对照原文判：一位说这是两个能分别押注的题，另一位说是同一件事的两面，放一张卡就够。…你怎么看：这类情况应该算一个题还是两个题？\"\n  - Options: one question, change 3 dropped (recommended): \"第二件事作为同一题的背景留着（后面判断时显示为'不判'），第三处改动作废。理由：都是同一个押注的不同侧面；我们的原则是偏谨慎、不要把一件事拆成碎题。\"; two questions, change 3 continues; case by case.\n  - Alex: \"算一个题，第三处不改 (Recommended)\".\n- **Asked:** \"第三处停下后，这两处的小测试（42 次发送，约 0.6 美元，上限 2 美元）要不要照常跑？\" Options: run (recommended): \"这两处不依赖第三处。任何一项不过就停，报给你。\"; wait. Alex: \"照常跑 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided:** a second side of the same bet (the shortage beside the shipments, the AI-chip share beside the chip total, the capacity keeping pace beside the demand) is one question; it stays as context in that question and is shown as not judged (D397). Change 3 (the `outcome` definition) is dropped, and the \"two bets in one thesis\" class is closed as not a Step 1 defect under this ruling. G1-a and G1-b run as fixed in `COMBINED-PLAN.md`; the candidate for later gates is c8 with changes 1 and 2 only.\n- **Scope:** clean Step 1; c8 stays in force.\n\n## D437 · 2026-11-13 · Carry changes 1 and 2 to gate 2 although the year line was missed\n\n- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/G1A-READING.md` and `G1B-READING.md`: \"第一关的结果：'客户那句'的改动过了；'今年明年各开一题'没过。…新版 9 次里只有 5 次把两年分开开题，事先定的线是 9 次至少 8 次。旧版 c8 是 0 次。…新写法 26 次里 20 次分开，旧版 26 次里 0 次。没分开的那几次，模型都读到了规则，但觉得'两年都开太多了'，只留一年。下一步怎么走？\"\n  - Options: carry both changes to gate 2 (recommended by Claude): \"分年虽然没达线，但从 0 次升到大约四分之三，而且'两年塞一题'完全消失，没发现带坏别的东西。第二关在存档上查它会不会弄坏周边情况（重复文章、同一量的另一种口径、延期的事等，约 1.5 美元，线先给你看）。代价：等于在看到结果后放宽了我自己定的线。\"; stop the year change and carry only the customer sentence (the reviewer, `council/lx-codex.md`, recommended stopping the year change and keeping c8); stop both and keep c8.\n  - Alex: \"带着两处改动进第二关 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided:** the candidate for gate 2 is c15yc (c8 with the year boundary and the scoped capacity counterexample). The year line's failure stays recorded as a failure (5 of 9 against 8 of 9); it is not presented as a pass. Gate 2's lines are written, reviewed and shown to Alex before any send. c8 stays in force.\n- **Scope:** clean Step 1.\n\n## D438 · 2026-11-13 · Send gate 2\n\n- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/GATE2.md` (version 11, reviewed clean in `council/mi-codex.md`): \"第二关审完了，要发吗？…新版做错的次数比旧版多 3 次以上（9 次里），就停下报给你。共 126 次发送，约 1.8 美元，上限 2.2 美元。\" Options: send (recommended): \"先跑完 126 次。我和一位盲读者各自逐条读，有分歧的一律算新版错。任何一条停止线被触发就停下报给你；全过的话再设计第三关（在新文章上新旧版对比），也先给你看。\"; do not send.\n- Alex: \"发 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided:** gate 2 is sent as written; a fired stop or an unexercised control goes to Alex; a pass leads to gate 3's design, shown to him before any send. c8 stays in force.\n\n## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n\n- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n## D547 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the audit of line 2 finds an undefined term; the description-only reading is refused; the recount against D397, D436 and the July rulings opens no prompt change (council consensus)\n\n- **The audit** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh-ladders/PROMPT-AUDIT-LINE-2.md`; the model's account on four stored\n  attempts, $0.0022 of a $0.05 ceiling; spend recorded under D439 about $18.43 of $40): the request of the answer-choice step\n  says \"List every other part of the topic's wording\" in four places and never says which field of the topic that is; every\n  failed attempt of the fresh week concerns a clause that sits only in the `outcome` field (listed 11 of 18 times; a clause in\n  the `description` 6 of 6); the model quotes the same sentence each time and mostly reads the wording as the description alone.\n- **Claude's recommendation, refused:** to rule that the wording is the description, so that outcome-only clauses need not be\n  listed and the six marks fall. The council (`reflection-2/cold-codex-6.md`): D397 judges the main part and shows the rest as\n  unjudged, and D436 (Alex: \"算一个题，第三处不改\") keeps a second side of the same bet \"as context in that question ... shown as\n  not judged\", in a case where that side sits in the outcome; the field cannot alone decide. The accounts are prompted and are\n  leads. The original marks are preserved and the ambiguity recorded.\n- **The recount the council set** (section 7 of the audit, $0): in the July full run's reading (91 ladders, third readers of\n  both families), an unlisted comparison with the reference figure was passed in 9 attempts on 4 theses, twice by an explicit\n  ruling of both third readers; an unlisted consequence clause was passed twice by both first readers; a difference inside an\n  outcome was never left unlisted; July's own failures of the line are a second figure or event of the topic's question left\n  out (2 or 3 of 91). So of the fresh week's six failures: two are a case the July rulings pass, two are disputed, two stand, on\n  one question.\n- **Decided, citing D439:** no omission recurs on two distinct questions under an agreed reading: no prompt change is designed\n  and the frozen step is untouched. The undefined term and the three remaining marks stay recorded. Sensitivity only, verdicts\n  unchanged: the fresh week's line 2 fails on 6 attempts as marked and on 2 to 4 under the July rulings; its questions right in\n  two of three attempts are 4 of 7 as marked and 5 or 6 of 7 under them.\n\n## D548 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the gates the new system must pass are listed as they stand in the record; the first blocker is the worthwhile questions its answer-choice step declines, framed at $0 (council consensus)\n\n- **Why:** D544 says \"until the new system passes its gates\" and lists none. Claude's draft table read the use-oriented\n  acceptance (D484) as the gate in force with the earlier ones as its components. The council\n  (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-2/cold-codex-7.md`) corrected it from the record: D483 says the added\n  acceptance changes no existing gate by itself, and D487 approves a lean comparison without replacing Stage A, Stage B or D427.\n- **Decided, citing D439:** the gates in force, in order: (1) Stage A on Alex's lines (D400), not passed; the 32 and 26 used on\n  the 40 July topics are the council's scaled diagnostic, not his numbers; (2) Stage B on D428's lines, not passed; (3) the\n  end-to-end comparison of D427 and D431 with Step 2's three checks, still owed, with \"beats\" not yet defined in numbers;\n  (4) use on unseen news, opened by Alex beside the others, its lines proposed and not his, not an accepted gate; (5)\n  integration and release, its acceptance not written and not invented now. The recount of D547 is confirmed as a sensitivity\n  reading that stops that wording change and passes nothing.\n- **The first blocker and its first step:** the new system cannot yet turn enough of its own worthwhile questions into valid\n  answer choices. A frame is written at $0 (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md`), ending in an answer\n  to one bounded question from the existing July refusal review: can a general, permitted change recover a worthwhile question\n  the system declines without making it answer questions it should refuse; one candidate named only if the records establish a\n  general mechanism and a test that protects the right refusals; otherwise \"no candidate\" and the council ranks the next\n  blocker. The credit-support amount is not ranked first (its fresh-week answer was unsupported for one reader family only;\n  guessed ranges are allowed under D398); it and the delivery gap stay recorded as product concerns.\n\n## D549 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: \"no candidate\" for the declined questions; one more week of news is prepared for a diagnostic reading of the answer choices, the send conditional on exposure, price and run checks (council consensus)\n\n- **The bounded question of D548, answered from the records** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md` section 2):\n  no candidate. The memory-price refusals come from the first step's shape of the topic (its two candidates failed; its sentence\n  changes on those articles are stopped; a rolling window is declined by Alex's ruling, D417); the rental-price refusals come\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/proofs/audit-cases.json\\\")); print(list(p)); [print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",k, json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)) for k,v in p.items() if \\\"reference\\\" in k]' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/proofs/audit-cases.json\\\")); print(list(p)); [print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",k, json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)) for k,v in p.items() if \\\"reference\\\" in k]' \"","aggregated_output":"['event_reference_cases_failed_or_open', 'event_answers_with_no_reference_that_both_families_held_sample', 'event_answers_with_a_quoted_reference_that_both_families_held_sample', 'unlisted_parts_new_agreed_cases', 'every_topic_of_the_week_with_what_each_attempt_listed']\n\n event_reference_cases_failed_or_open [\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u1/clean-11\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will China's government approve imports of Nvidia's H200 AI chips into China — and roughly how many — enabling Nvidia to begin generating H200 revenue in the country?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Chinese authorities grant approval for Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek and other firms to import Nvidia H200 chips (potentially a total below 200,000), as reflected in official Chinese government decisions and in Nvidia's disclosed China H200 revenue.\",\n   \"period\": \"Nvidia's current fiscal year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027), checked at its next annual report/10-K; set by the rule that a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n   \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n   \"sentence\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site.\\nChinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\\nThe companies need to say how many chips they need – and why – to get approval, according to the Information.\\nThe chips have emerged as a geopolitical flas\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities officially approve at least one application by Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek, or another Chinese firm to import Nvidia H200 chips into China by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The reference is null even though the article reports that China plans to allow limited H200 purchases.\",\n     \"XR: the reference is null although the article states 'China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips', a stated plan.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u1/clean-6\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Rubin Ultra rack-scale platform — the Kyber NVL144 architecture that houses 144 Rubin Ultra GPUs — reach first shipments in 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform reaches first shipments (the step that brings revenue) in 2027 or is delayed to 2028.\",\n   \"period\": \"2028 — the release date SemiAnalysis reports Kyber has been pushed to from an original 2027; the question is settled when Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra first ships (the item supports the original-2027-vs-2028 timing).\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia pushes Kyber release to 2028 following manufacturing concerns – report\",\n   \"sentence\": \"The Kyber server cabinets, which have been designed to house 144 Rubin Ultra GPUs connected via the company’s NVLink 7 Switch, had originally been slated for release in 2027.\\nKyber allows GPUs to be mounted in compute trays that sit vertically rather than horizontally, a design that Nvidia has described as being “like books on a shelf,” and which reportedly boosts density and reduces latency.\\nHowever, the research firm claimed that issues in manufacturing the printed circuit board (PCB) midplane that connects the modules together have caused the setback.\\n“Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has bee\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform make its first shipments during calendar 2027, as established by an NVIDIA shipment confirmation or a SemiAnalysis follow-up report?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": \"had originally been slated for release in 2027\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": \"had originally been slated for release in 2027\",\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"holds\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"open\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The reference quotes a 2027 release plan but omits its stated year, and the 2028 due date leaves a 2027 shipment question open for an extra year.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": \"pushing its release date to 2028\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u3/clean-3\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform, the product line that carries its data center value, begin shipping by a check date (end of calendar 2026)?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Confirmation that first Vera Rubin shipments have begun, versus slipping into 2027 or later.\",\n   \"period\": \"First shipments by end of calendar 2026 — set by the item: the platform 'could begin shipping later this year' in an article dated 2 July 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n   \"sentence\": \"Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform by December 31, 2026, as determined from NVIDIA earnings releases and Form 10-Q disclosures and first-shipment confirmations from NVIDIA or its server and system partners?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The article says Vera Rubin could begin shipping later this year, but the reference is null.\",\n     \"XR: the reference is null although the article states the expected timing in words (Vera Rubin 'is in full production and could begin shipping later this year'), which the field should quote with kind expected and no number.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u3/clean-9\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices with an adverse decision, fine or remedy, and by when?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The French competition authority's conclusion of its antitrust probe into Nvidia's alleged anti-competitive conduct in cloud-AI and GPU markets, including the decision date, finding and any fine or remedy imposed.\",\n   \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027) — set because a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end; the item reports the probe is 'nearing a conclusion.'\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n   \"sentence\": \"Regulators are simultaneously intensifying their oversight, with the French competition authority announcing Thursday that its antitrust investigation into the company is nearing a conclusion.\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"holds\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"open\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"XR: the reference is null although the article states the authority announced its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', an expectation stated in words.