\"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The article says the French competition authority announced that its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion'. That is a stated expectation of a near-term decision, and the reference should quote it in words, but the field is null.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The article states the French competition authority announced that its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', a stated expectation of a decision, yet the reference is null.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"XR: the article says the authority announced that its investigation is 'nearing a conclusion', which is a stated expectation for this event, yet the reference is null.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c3/clean-12\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will France's competition authority (Autorité de la concurrence) conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by issuing a formal decision — a statement of objections, fine or behavioural remedies — rather than closing the case without action?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A formal decision, or closure without action, by the French competition authority in its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's alleged anti-competitive practices in cloud-AI and GPU markets, including any fine or remedy imposed.\",\n   \"period\": \"Nvidia's fiscal year ending late January 2027 (FY2027, reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision because the item gives no date beyond the authority's Thursday announcement.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n   \"sentence\": \"Regulators are simultaneously intensifying their oversight, with the French competition authority announcing Thursday that its antitrust investigation into the company is nearing a conclusion.\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding its antitrust investigation into Nvidia by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The article says the authority announced its investigation is 'nearing a conclusion', which states an expectation in words, yet the reference is null.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"XR: the article says the authority announced that its investigation is 'nearing a conclusion', which is a stated expectation for this event, yet the reference is null.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The article reports the authority's own announcement that its investigation 'is nearing a conclusion', an expectation for this event that the reference should quote, yet the reference is null.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"the week of 10-06\",\n  \"case\": \"c1/clean-7\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Rubin data center GPU — the next generation of the product that carries Nvidia's data center revenue — reach volume ramp in the quarter management describes, or slip into calendar 2027 because of memory shortages?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Rubin's volume ramp and shipments occur in the quarter Nvidia describes (about 20% of data center revenue) or are pushed into calendar 2027, and whether reported sales timing slips.\",\n   \"period\": \"Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) and fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027), which will show whether the Rubin ramp landed by the quarter ending late January 2027 or slid into calendar 2027, the two points the item frames ('this quarter' versus 'slip into 2027').\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-10-07\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia (NVDA): Is There Still Room to Run?\",\n   \"sentence\": \"Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter, and industry reports say the ramp could slip into 2027 because of memory shortages.\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia reach volume ramp for Rubin during the fiscal quarter ending in late January 2027, as shown by its fiscal Q4 FY2027 earnings release and shipment disclosures?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"holds\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"open\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"Q: the outcome names 'the quarter Nvidia describes', the article's 'this quarter' (fiscal Q3 FY2027, ending late October 2026), but the question asks about 'the fiscal quarter ending in late January 2027', which also takes in January 2027 that the thesis counts as the slip into calendar 2027; XR: the reference is null although the article states the expectation 'should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter'.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": \"should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter\",\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"holds\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"open\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The question requires both Nvidia and server makers to confirm shipments rather than asking whether shipments occurred in the named quarter; February 24 is not a stated check day, and the 20% revenue-share expectation is not an expectation for the ramp event.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": \"should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter\",\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"holds\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": [\n     \"holds\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"mark\": \"open\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"The question permits a ramp through January 31 instead of asking whether it occurred in the described quarter, February 28 is not a stated check day, and the 20% revenue-share expectation is not an expectation for the ramp event.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"the week of 10-06\",\n  \"case\": \"c1/clean-9\",\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Groq 3 LPX rack-scale LPU system — the first product built on the Groq technology it paid about $20 billion to license and staff — reach volume shipments and commercial scale in the quarter Nvidia describes (its fiscal Q3 FY2027), or slip?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Groq 3 LPX volume shipments occur 'later this quarter' as Nvidia stated, and whether the system begins contributing to reported data center revenue or slips into fiscal Q4 FY2027/calendar 2027.\",\n   \"period\": \"Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) confirming shipments in the quarter Nvidia described in the Oct. 8, 2026 item; if unconfirmed there, the fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027) fixes the slip.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia (NVDA)’s $20 Billion Groq Deal Faces a Legal Test. Does It Matter for NVDA’s Valuation?\",\n   \"sentence\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) said Groq 3 LPX, its first rack-scale LPU system combining Nvidia's high-throughput architecture with Groq's high-interactivity technology, is already in full production, with volume shipments expected later this quarter.\"\n  },\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Groq 3 LPX rack-scale system make volume shipments during fiscal Q3 FY2027, as confirmed by NVIDIA's Q3 FY2027 report or a shipment confirmation from NVIDIA or its system partners?\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"reference_words\": \"volume shipments expected later this quarter\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"reference_words\": null,\n    \"first_readers_codex_claude\": [\n     \"fails\",\n     \"fails\"\n    ],\n    \"third_readers_claude_codex\": null,\n    \"mark\": \"fails\",\n    \"failing_readers_reasons\": [\n     \"November 30 is not a stated assessment day, and the reference omits Nvidia's expectation of volume shipments later that quarter.\",\n     \"XR: the article states the expectation in the words 'volume shipments expected later this quarter', so the reference should quote it as expected and not be null.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"reference_words\": \"volume shipments expected later this quarter\",\n    \"mark\": \"holds\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n\n event_answers_with_no_reference_that_both_families_held_sample [\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u3/clean-5\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make and disclose sales of H200 AI chips to Chinese commercial customers by FY2027 year-end (2027-01-31), as shown by Nvidia disclosures or confirmation of the sales?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"acc/clean-2\",\n  \"attempt\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA complete the announced acquisition of Hugging Face by 2028-03-05, as verified by NVIDIA’s filings or transaction announcements?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c2/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA report or otherwise confirm in its Form 10-Q, Form 10-K, or management commentary that it recorded China data-center revenue from H200 shipments by January 31, 2027?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c3/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"Will the US export-control authorization allowing Nvidia to sell semiconductors to China under specified conditions remain in force, be broadened, or be tightened by 2027-01-31?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u2/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will the Chinese government permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips in mainland China by January 31, 2027, as shown by an official Chinese government or regulatory announcement, or by NVIDIA disclosing H2\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u3/clean-9\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will the Autorité de la concurrence publish a decision or conclusion on its investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u2/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"Will the Chinese government or a competent Chinese regulator officially authorize H200 sales into mainland China by January 31, 2027?\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c1/clean-5\",\n  \"attempt\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly announce a finding, penalty, or new export-control measure stemming from its investigation into DeepSeek’s access to restr\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u2/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"Will China’s government permit NVIDIA to sell H200 chips in mainland China by January 31, 2027, as shown by an official Chinese announcement or NVIDIA disclosure that H200 sales or shipments have resu\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u1/clean-12\",\n  \"attempt\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"Will France’s Autorité de la concurrence publish a decision or conclusion ending its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU-market practices by January 31, 2027?\"\n }\n]\n\n event_answers_with_a_quoted_reference_that_both_families_held_sample [\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u1/clean-3\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin first shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by NVIDIA disclosures or shipping confirmations?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u3/clean-7\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack system for the Rubin Ultra generation during calendar 2028, as determined by Nvidia shipment confirmations and data-center product commentary \",\n  \"reference_words\": \"had been slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra, Nvidia's next-generation rack-scale system, in 2027 .\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"the week of 10-06\",\n  \"case\": \"c1/clean-5\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia close its acquisition of Hugging Face by June 30, 2027, as verified by Nvidia's closing announcement?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"anticipated to occur in the first half of 2027\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u2/clean-5\",\n  \"attempt\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"Will the first shipment of NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system paired with Vera Rubin Ultra occur by December 31, 2027, as confirmed by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"had been slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra, Nvidia's next-generation rack-scale system, in 2027\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u2/clean-2\",\n  \"attempt\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform make its first shipments by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by an NVIDIA disclosure or official shipment announcement?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"could begin shipping later this year\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"Alex's 44 topics\",\n  \"case\": \"u1/clean-6\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform during calendar 2027, as confirmed by NVIDIA or reported by SemiAnalysis?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"had originally been slated for release in 2027\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c3/clean-6\",\n  \"attempt\": 2,\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm that it has made first customer shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture (Vera Rubin Ultra generation) by December 31, 2028, in a quarterly report, management statement, pro\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"had been slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra, Nvidia's next-generation rack-scale system, in 2027\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n },\n {\n  \"reading\": \"July\",\n  \"case\": \"c3/clean-6\",\n  \"attempt\": 3,\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm first customer shipments of its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation by December 31, 2028?\",\n  \"reference_words\": \"had been slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra, Nvidia's next-generation rack-scale system, in 2027 .\",\n  \"kind\": \"expected\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '60,125p' clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '60,125p' clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"- A company's figure runs from Strongly bullish to Strongly bearish, meaning good or bad for the company's business. An event's\n  rungs carry no such labels.\n- The reference is what the question is measured against when it opens. Its kind is `expected` for what the market expects: a\n  consensus, the company's guidance, a stated plan or deadline. For a figure, where the article states no expectation and gives\n  the amount most recently reported for the same quantity, that amount is the reference and its kind is `last_reported`; a\n  reported amount is never called an expectation (D411). When the article states a number, the field carries it and a\n  figure's middle rung holds it; a stated range is carried by its two ends, and the middle rung runs from at or below its lower end to at or above its upper end. When the\n  article states it in words alone, the field carries the words and no number, and the ranges are the step's own estimate.\n- The due day is when the question can be resolved: a figure's publication date; for an event, the date its outcome is assessed. Where\n  the thesis or the article states the day a figure is published, that day is right. Where neither does (`due_day_basis` is\n  `expected_publication`), code sets the day and the step's own estimate is not shown: 60 days after the company's fiscal\n  year-end for a company's figure, 90 days after the calendar year-end for a theme's (D414). That day is right when the figure\n  is a figure for that year; it is wrong when the figure the question asks for is not a year's figure (a quarter, a survey's\n  rolling twelve months), which is then a fault of the question's period and of the due day both.\n- A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year is never a judged question: the step must decline it. A ladder written for\n  one is wrong even when it asks exactly what the thesis names (mark `Y`). An annual figure that only names quarterly reports as\n  the material that settles it is not such a case.\n- A step may decline (`no_ladder`) only in the seven cases its instructions allow: the thesis has no main figure or event (its\n  outcome names none, or several things and none is the main one); nothing in it can be checked on a date (for an event:\n  neither the thesis nor the article gives a date, and the thesis names no period, unless it is a pending regulatory decision,\n  which is due at the company's fiscal year-end); it is the company's figure for a\n  quarter or a half-year; it is a figure for a period that is not one fiscal or calendar year, such as a survey's rolling twelve\n  months, and neither the thesis nor the article gives the day it is published (D417); it is a figure for a year that had already\n  ended on the article's day; it is a figure for a year beyond\n  next year, unless the thesis's `opens_as` is binding_obligation; or the question belongs to another company, or to a matter that\n  none of the listed themes covers (the listed themes are given with the packet). Declining for any other reason, or when the case\n  named does not truly apply, is not justified.\n\n## What to return\n\nOne JSON object per item, one per line, in item order, as your final message: no prose before or after, no code fence. Fields:\n\n| field | values | the mark |\n|---|---|---|\n| `item` | the item number | |\n| `Q` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the judged question is worded as a question, not as an assertion, and asks the thing the thesis's `outcome` names. For a figure it also names the period the figure covers, or the day it is measured at, and the material that settles it. And it does not ask something other than its `focus` line (a focus that also names parts listed in `not_judged` is expected and is not a conflict). It can be understood by a reader who never sees the article: it never says \"this item\" or leans on a figure or a name it does not give. A group named as the trade names it (\"the big four AI hyperscalers\", \"the top five hyperscalers\") is a name the question gives: a question is not failed for not listing the group's members. `n/a` for a `no_ladder` |\n| `O` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the object is the question's own company or the right theme, by the rule above: a tracked government decision on a class of products is the theme's; the company's own sales under it, and a proceeding against the company, are the company's |\n| `R` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | exactly one rung holds for every outcome. For a figure: the ranges meet end to end. For an event, where code writes the last rung: the `Yes` condition is the event the question asks about; the first sentence of the `Ruled out` condition, when there is one, is a decision against that event as a whole, or its abandonment or withdrawal as a whole, taken after the article's day and standing on the due day, and not the event's merely being still awaited, the refusal of one part of it, or a bar already in place when the article appeared (it need not list every way: code's sentence takes the others); and where the event can plainly be ruled out before the due day (a formal refusal, a block, an announced abandonment; for an authority's proceeding, its formal abandonment or withdrawal without the asked-for decision or conclusion) and the answer has no `Ruled out` rung, the mark fails; it fails too when `ruled_out_by` names no one who decides, or when the decision named is the day arriving, the event not having happened, or a decision to go on with a proceeding. Every condition is concrete and can be checked on the due day: none rests on a target or a threshold that is not yet set |\n| `D` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the due day follows the rule for its kind. A figure: the day the thesis or the article states, or, where neither states one, the day code sets from the year the figure covers (60 days after the company's fiscal year-end; 90 days after the calendar year-end for a theme's figure), which holds when the figure asked for is that year's figure. An event: the date the thesis or the article gives for assessing it, or the last day of the period it names, or the company's fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision with no date. It fails when the day contradicts a date the thesis or the article gives, falls before the figure's period ends, or, for an event, is a date none of these gives And `due_day_basis` says truly where the day comes from: `stated` only when the thesis or the article gives that day; `period_end` only when it is the last day of the period the thesis names, or the fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision; `expected_publication` when the step set the day it expects the figure to be published. For a thesis whose `opens_as` is binding_obligation: an obligation already taken on is due at its next annual filing, and one not yet signed on the day by which the signing can be checked; another day fails |\n| `X` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | a figure: a number the `reference` carries lies in the middle rung, as the judge will read it (for a stated range: the middle rung runs from at or below its lower end to at or above its upper end); a reference with no number, or none, has nothing to place and holds, unless the ladder presents as expected something the article does not state. An event: the ladder presents as expected only what the article states |\n| `F` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a company's figure only: the direction is defensible (which end is bullish), and the reason given in `favourable_why` supports the favourable end. For an amount the company owes, guarantees or has committed to pay, where neither the thesis nor the article settles which end is good for the business (they argue both ends or say nothing on it), the lower end is the favourable one (D413), and \"higher\" fails unless the thesis's own words say that more of it is good. `n/a` for an event and for a theme |\n| `Y` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a figure only: the year, the unit and the scale of the numbers are the question's (an amount in full; a percentage as 31, not 0.31), and the figure is a whole year's. A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year fails, whatever the thesis asks |\n| `G` | `holds`, `fails`, `not_assessable`, `n/a` | for a figure, always one of the first three: where the article gives any figure for this quantity, `holds` when an analyst would accept the ranges as a fair division of the outcomes around it and `fails` when not; `not_assessable` when the article gives none. `n/a` only for an event's ladder and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `L` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | every other part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) is listed in `not_judged`, each with a reason that says why it is left out; a wording that asks nothing else holds with an empty list |\n| `B` | a list | exactly one entry for each part listed in `not_judged`, in its order: `\"bet\"` when an analyst would hold a separate view on it, `\"not_a_bet\"` when it is a detail of the judged question; `[]` when nothing is listed and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `XR` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the `reference` field quotes what the article states the market expects, with `kind` `expected`, or, for a figure where the article states no expectation, the amount most recently reported for the same quantity (the same thing measured the same way: not a part of it, a ceiling on it or another quantity), with `kind` `last_reported`; the kind says truly which. It carries the number when the article states one (a range by its two ends), and no number the article does not state. It is null only when the article states no expectation and, for a figure, no amount last reported for the same quantity either; an event's is null whenever the article states no expectation |\n| `N` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a `no_ladder` only: the refusal is justified by one of the allowed cases, and that case truly applies. A refusal because the question belongs to another company or to a matter no listed theme covers names that company or matter. Which year is this year and which next year is read from the `fiscal_year_note` |\n| `W` | a string | any other fault that would mislead a reader of this judged question, in a short sentence; the empty string `\"\"` when there is none. The field is always present |\n| `why` | a string | one sentence giving the reason for every `fails` and for a non-empty `W`, naming the words or the figure; it may be empty only when no mark fails and `W` is empty |\n\nRead each item's article before answering it. Judge only what is in the item.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
